<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>GoVariableDeclaration - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/govariabledeclaration/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/govariabledeclaration/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 224</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_224/</link><pubDate>Mon, 05 May 2025 15:15:46 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_224/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;In the following code, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is declared, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared. Determine whether each statement is correct.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;1 x, _:= f()&#10;2 x,_ = f()&#10;3 x, y := f()&#10;4 x, y = f()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&#10;Variable declaration. 1. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is already declared, so &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; cannot be used; 2. Correct; 3. Correct, when assigning multiple values, at least one variable on the left side of &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; must be undeclared; 4. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 161</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_161/</link><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jan 2025 21:10:21 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_161/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;In the following code, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is declared, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared. Determine whether each statement is correct.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;1）x, _ := f()&#10;2）x, _ = f()&#10;3）x, y := f()&#10;4）x, y = f()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 class="heading-element" id="1-x-_--f"&gt;&lt;span&gt;1. &lt;code&gt;x, _ := f()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#1-x-_--f" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incorrect&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 145</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_145/</link><pubDate>Sat, 28 Dec 2024 12:34:35 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_145/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;To define a package-level global string variable, which of the following syntax is correct (multiple choice):&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. var str string&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. str := &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;D. var str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;A, D&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Only &lt;code&gt;var&lt;/code&gt; can be used for global definitions.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;B: Only supports local variable declaration.&#10;C: Assignment, not definition.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 131</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_131/</link><pubDate>Sat, 14 Dec 2024 11:59:22 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_131/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Regarding channels, which of the following syntax is correct:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. var ch chan int&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. ch := make(chan int)&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. &amp;lt;- ch&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;D. ch &amp;lt;-&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;A, B, C&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A declares variable &lt;code&gt;ch&lt;/code&gt; of type &lt;code&gt;chan int&lt;/code&gt;, but does not initialize it.&#10;B declares variable &lt;code&gt;ch&lt;/code&gt; of type &lt;code&gt;chan int&lt;/code&gt;, and initializes it.&#10;C reads from the channel, discarding the value.&#10;D is incorrect; writing to a channel requires a value.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 120</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_120/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 23:43:03 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_120/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;In the following code, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is declared, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared. Determine whether each statement is correct.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;A: x, _ := f()&#10;B: x, _ = f()&#10;C: x, y := f()&#10;D: x, y = f()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;A is wrong, B is correct, C is correct, D is wrong.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 085</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_085/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:45:11 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_085/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Which of the following options is correct?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#10; if a := 1; false {&#10; } else if b := 2; false {&#10; } else {&#10; println(a, b)&#10; }&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;A. 1 2&#10;B. compilation error&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Involves code block issues.&#10;For details, you can refer to this article:&#10;&lt;a href="https://studygolang.com/articles/35587" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://studygolang.com/articles/35587&lt;/a&gt;&#10;After expanding, the code becomes:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;{&#10; a := 1&#10; if false {&#10;&#10; } else {&#10; b := 2&#10; if false {&#10;&#10; } else {&#10; println(a, b)&#10; }&#10; }&#10; }&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/details&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 070</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_070/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:53 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_070/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;In the following code, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is declared, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared. Determine whether each statement is correct.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;x, &lt;em&gt;:= f()&#10;x,&lt;/em&gt; = f()&#10;x, y := f()&#10;x, y = f()&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&#10;Variable declaration. 1. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is already declared, so &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; cannot be used; 2. Correct; 3. Correct, when assigning multiple values, at least one variable on the left side of &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; must be undeclared; 4. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 053</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_053/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:33 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_053/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;To define a package-level global string variable, which of the following syntax is correct (multiple choice):&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A. var str string&#10;B. str := &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&#10;C. str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&#10;D. var str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;A, D&#10;The key is &amp;ldquo;package-level global&amp;rdquo;.&#10;B: &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; can only be used inside functions.&#10;C: This is an assignment, not a declaration.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 039</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_039/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:16 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_039/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Regarding channels, which of the following syntax is correct:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;A. var ch chan int&#10;B. ch := make(chan int)&#10;C. &amp;lt;- ch&#10;D. ch &amp;lt;-&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Answer: ABC&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A and B both declare a channel; C reads from a channel;&#10;Writing to a channel must include a value, so D is incorrect.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 022</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_022/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 19:49:56 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_022/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Will the following code compile? If so, what will be the output?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#10;&#10;var(&#10; size := 1024&#10; max_size = size*2&#10;)&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10; fmt.Println(size,max_size)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Answer: No.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;var(&#10; size := 1024&#10;)&#10;Does not conform to specification.&#10;Problem 1: `var` variable declaration cannot use `:=`.&#10;Problem 2: `:=` can only be used inside a function; this problem uses it for declaring global variables.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reference Analysis: The main point of this problem is the short variable declaration mode, such as: &lt;code&gt;x := 100&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>